  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_5ddd79c3299040c9911ae75928c0865d",
      "statement": "Request IDs are constructed as `traceLinkType.getKeyPrefix() + \":\" + projectName + <hash>` in `AbstractController.generateRequestId`, where the hash is a UUID-from-bytes hash (MD5-based name UUID) over the concatenated input files, produced by `HashGenerator.getMD5HashFromFiles`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/controller/AbstractController.java#L131-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:78d9b6a73f688485eab23b162556e28436c234b264e7f4ee0808bc3f74dd5f80:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/util/HashGenerator.java#L27-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc7cedeb69c49b34a753558863fb4f0965d296a7814ca264bddb9a2674efbfc3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_84f9db8f2a21416f93d4eee2d0415ae9",
      "statement": "The hash input is the raw bytes of all input files concatenated by `FileConverter.convertFilesToByte` (in list order, without separators, file names not included); an empty file list raises `FileNotFoundException` and an unreadable file raises `FileConversionException`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/converter/FileConverter.java#L34-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1acd981accfae3dd52fdff8903b42f2c92a27886f545eac8102fb295e0af9111:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/util/HashGenerator.java#L27-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc7cedeb69c49b34a753558863fb4f0965d296a7814ca264bddb9a2674efbfc3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_28344788454e4847bcef4c3d9921805a",
      "statement": "The optional `additionalConfigs` JSON is deliberately not hashed into the request ID; requests that differ only in configuration collide on the same ID and within the TTL window are served the cached result computed with the first request's configuration. This is documented in architecture_decisions.md as a known limitation that may be revisited.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://architecture_decisions.md#L82-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f5c75761030041b3f3df29b9f70aebeda6b8c747ba2047abbef4a0a4f0554c1c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/controller/AbstractController.java#L131-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:78d9b6a73f688485eab23b162556e28436c234b264e7f4ee0808bc3f74dd5f80:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a29dd390d3e54c6489339fb7cce23eb7",
      "statement": "Each `TraceLinkType` carries a `keyPrefix` (ardocodeResult, arcotlResult, swattrResult, transarcResult) used as the ID prefix; `TraceLinkType.fromId(id)` matches `id.startsWith(keyPrefix)` to recover the type (falling back to `OTHER`), and `ArdocoResultResponse` uses it to derive the `traceLinkType` field of responses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/api_response/ArdocoResultResponse.java#L34-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e11a9cbb3e2ff693771118b1496f26b3b5dce1bfa3c6ef516a835d6aa1fd0864:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/api_response/TraceLinkType.java#L9-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f667cff4f73cd1f9a3dee71d3584210c38769a9e12684aa5b3b7b82791f6e161:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_db13307de5a348e483ea8574a949f020",
      "statement": "`InconsistencyController` overrides `generateRequestId` to produce `swattrResultInconsistency:<projectName><hash>`, so inconsistency results are keyed separately from plain SWATTR results despite sharing the `SAD_SAM` TraceLinkType and the same input files.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/controller/InconsistencyController.java#L143-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a13e6f0eeeeb06c99560ba3e6bb5c1c50be916604eea7b5f9c6bd33b63d31a29:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_46f0161cf81f49d499e7439e0851a602",
      "statement": "`RedisAccessor.saveResult` stores every result under the request ID as a plain string with an expiry taken from `redis.time-to-live.hours` (24 hours by default in application.properties), so Redis entries expire after 24h and the key population stays small.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/repository/RedisAccessor.java#L26-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5631743329d8f003fce26207ca8a9be2efb032c5cdb5af1f1fd5d9d774bc246:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.properties#L10-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e1c8b462954dbaec1982b906567215af4c4c346e97a87e58623d0180ff8a4916:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8be52bec7ae94fc39fcff0d16a37a2aa",
      "statement": "The large MD5-based UUID hash space (collision probability almost zero) combined with the automatic 24h TTL is what makes content-based key reuse safe; after TTL expiry the key is gone, so a re-request with the same inputs re-runs the pipeline and returns the same ID as if it were new.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://architecture_decisions.md#L82-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8ab7ceee6f728d39968f1efcf06d4a9c989a337fd12a78830b3ea1f4e2e8c7c4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractRunnerTLRService.java#L83-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e8428ca1e5f1259866bc20abc8cfbf6a42fec3c0ee5cba8a6c9b5589b744a11:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_13eb28ed7073424090c9fecd837d1916",
      "statement": "`AbstractRunnerTLRService.runPipeline` implements the dedup decision: a result already in Redis is returned directly, an in-flight result suppresses a new run, and only when neither is true is a fresh run dispatched via `CompletableFuture.supplyAsync` and its future registered under the request ID in `CurrentlyRunningRequestsRepository`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractRunnerTLRService.java#L83-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e8428ca1e5f1259866bc20abc8cfbf6a42fec3c0ee5cba8a6c9b5589b744a11:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b240f63fd78543fb8c14e927c5505b0a",
      "statement": "The cached-or-in-flight check in `runPipeline` is not atomic (check-then-act), so two concurrent first requests for the same brand-new ID can each dispatch a run before either future is registered; the system converges because the later `saveResult` overwrites the earlier result, but one run may be wasted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractRunnerTLRService.java#L83-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e8428ca1e5f1259866bc20abc8cfbf6a42fec3c0ee5cba8a6c9b5589b744a11:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d6a2270debde47138c0096fdc563fe3e",
      "statement": "On pipeline failure, `runPipelineAsync` stores `\"Error: \" + message` under the request ID with the normal 24h TTL instead of leaving the key absent; a re-request within that window hits the cached error marker, which `getResultFromDatabase` surfaces as an `ArdocoException` (HTTP 500) rather than re-running the pipeline.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractRunnerTLRService.java#L102-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44663f46d4490d4d47e0a1684038f70084ec073f6b4f0d47534a4d3b380fd4a5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractService.java#L58-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2e1e1ed3cd0f52f012924132fb5b5d293dc7b7385d53c05143ec8eb101cb0482:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0010e15475b344d796b8d446823e5a86",
      "statement": "Because IDs are self-describing via their key prefix, results from any family can be retrieved through the cross-family `/api/get-result/{id}` and `/api/wait-for-result/{id}` endpoints of `ResultController`; `waitForResult` blocks on the registered future with a timeout from `tlr.timeout.seconds` (60 seconds by default), yielding `202 Accepted` on timeout.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/controller/ResultController.java#L40-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:90c5e30d9f87b7762b58fbc20733c363639b406d8021cea10b1f713628e63f25:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/ResultService.java#L57-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4dd06ae1f77b7e09dc85db0fabc8a16aca983e1cd1f1cd9c6619b5487a3504eb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.properties#L21-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f06c9a644f89cda988510d8174650f35fb795c82b776a5b457b288f8454c670a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5d7b27470ed5483d84325518834aae61",
      "statement": "The behavior is covered by focused tests: `HashGeneratorTest` verifies equal hashes for equal file contents and error paths, `RedisAccessorTest` verifies the Redis key-value semantics (including overwrite) against a real `redis:7.0-alpine` Testcontainers container, and `AbstractTLRControllerTest` verifies the full start-poll-retrieve flow including that re-starting the same pipeline returns the same ID with the result present in the database.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/test/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/controller/AbstractTLRControllerTest.java#L89-L106",
